Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 18 — Android Wear OS, Android TV, Android Auto & Embedded Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand Android applications designed for specialized Android platforms such as Wear OS, Android TV, Android Auto, Android Automotive OS (AAOS), Android Things (legacy), kiosks, point-of-sale terminals, smart displays, industrial devices, and other embedded Android systems. These applications differ significantly from phone apps in terms of lifecycle, input methods, hardware integration, UI paradigms, and platform APIs.



> Core Principle:
These are not "phone apps on different screens." They are platform-specific applications built around different interaction models, hardware capabilities, and operating system services. Recover the platform model before analyzing the application.




