Stage 27 — Common Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating specialized Android platforms as standard phone applications.

Ignoring platform-specific lifecycle behavior.

Assuming identical input models across devices.

Overlooking OEM-specific APIs and services.

Ignoring companion applications and cross-device communication.

Mixing framework infrastructure with application logic.



---

Stage 28 — Specialized Android Platform Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify and classify applications targeting Wear OS, Android TV, Android Auto, Android Automotive OS, and embedded Android platforms.

✅ Reconstruct platform-specific UI, lifecycle, input, navigation, and hardware integration.

✅ Analyze communication with companion devices, cloud services, vehicle systems, and embedded hardware.

✅ Understand platform services, background execution models, sensor integration, and persistence.

✅ Distinguish platform infrastructure from application-specific business logic.

✅ Validate architectural understanding through runtime observation.

✅ Produce comprehensive documentation describing the complete architecture, execution model, hardware interaction, and platform integration of specialized Android applications.



